 {
  "tab": "collaborations",
  "title": "Predicting new collaborations",
  "text": "What it does: for every pair of faculty who have not yet co-authored, the model reads their papers up to a given year (co-author network, research topics, shared references and citations, how recently each has published) and scores how likely the two are to start working together within 3 years. For each faculty member this gives a ranked list of suggested partners; the top 5 are what the dashboard and the assistant show. Results, tested only on years the model had not seen (2020, 2021, 2022 pooled): of the faculty who really started a new collaboration, 46% had a correct partner among their top 5 suggestions and 64% among their top 10. The ranking beats chance by about 30x (new collaborations are rare: 0.19% of pairs, 761 real ones among 404,282 pairs). The output is a ranking, not a probability.",
